     Oops. I checked the Makefile for 1.4f and I see it uses LFLAGS for 
the flags to pass to the loader, not LDFLAGS. (Looking at 3.4.2 I see it 
also uses LFLAGS.) So, this is my final answer (still without testing it 
on a Linux or *BSD system):

     gmake CFLAGS="-ansi" LFLAGS="-lcompat"

